= Ceramic
{parent=Materials science}

A <ceramic> is an inorganic, nonmetallic <solid>, often formed by heating and cooling. <Ceramics> may contain several <chemical compounds> and need not have a single <crystal structure>.

= Sintering
{parent=Materials science}

<Sintering> joins particles into a coherent <solid> by heating, sometimes with applied <pressure>, without completely <melting> the material. It is used to consolidate powders of <ceramics> and <metals>.

= Sputtering
{parent=Materials science}

<Sputtering> ejects surface <chemical atoms> from a <solid> through bombardment by energetic incident <particles>, often <ions>.

= Annealing
{disambiguate=materials science}
{parent=Materials science}

= Annealing
{synonym}

<Annealing> uses controlled heating and cooling to change a <solid>'s internal structure and properties. Its outcome depends on the <temperature>, duration and cooling history.

